WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:24.380
Hello.

9
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:25.940
Hi, everyone.

10
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.520
It is Money Part 2 today.

11
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:29.940
Second half of money.

12
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:31.620
Second half of money.

13
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.760
We got lots to cover.

14
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:38.820
It's Season 4, Episode 8, written by Paul Lieberstein, directed by Paul Lieberstein.

15
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.400
Angela, I'm coming in hot today, and I'm coming in right with a summary.

16
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.200
Are you ready?

17
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:43.920
Yeah.

18
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.080
No banter.

19
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.640
No banter at the top.

20
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:47.580
Okay.

21
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.080
Here we go.

22
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.040
All right.

23
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.220
In Money Part 1, we found out that Michael has money troubles.

24
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.880
He had to take a second job as a telemarketer.

25
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:03.680
Meanwhile, Pam and Jim visited Shrewt Farms, which Dwight has started operating as a bed and breakfaSt.

26
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.420
And Andy serenaded Angela in hopes of winning her heart.

27
00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.180
Well, this week, Michael works with Oscar to try and get himself out of debt.

28
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.200
Andy continues to pursue Angela.

29
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:22.400
And Kelly flunts her new relationship with Daryl in front of Ryan, who really just wants everyone in the office to use PowerPoint.

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.060
PowerPoint, PowerPoint, PowerPoint.

31
00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.780
Michael just thinks it's like a cheer from cheerleading camp.

32
00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.300
He's literally powerfully pointing his finger as he says it.

33
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:33.680
Yep.

34
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:34.320
All right.

35
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.760
Well, fast fact number one.

36
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:41.560
We mentioned last week that this was the first episode that was directed by Paul Lieberstein.

37
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:49.700
But I discovered in my research this week, Angela, that he was nominated for an Emmy Award for directing this episode.

38
00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:50.960
His first episode.

39
00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:51.740
Wow.

40
00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.860
Where do you go from there?

41
00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:55.900
You're like, I crushed it.

42
00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:56.580
I'm done.

43
00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.100
Yeah, pretty much.

44
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.320
Well, here's something crazy.

45
00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:07.860
He was up against Paul Feig, who was nominated for directing the season four finale Goodbye, Toby.

46
00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.500
But they both loSt.

47
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.140
Aw.

48
00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.440
To Barry Sonnenfeld for Pushing Daisies.

49
00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:14.220
Oh.

50
00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.100
I mean, Barry is a fantastic director.

51
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:16.580
I know.

52
00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:17.900
Well, dang it.

53
00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.940
We had a Paul versus Paul.

54
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:20.780
Yes.

55
00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:21.760
Who would have won?

56
00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.840
I would have been able to choose between those two guys.

57
00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:24.580
Yes.

58
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.280
Maybe better.

59
00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.120
Maybe better.

60
00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.660
You know, for our sake.

61
00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:28.860
Because it's about us.

62
00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:29.880
Maybe better.

63
00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:30.540
You know why?

64
00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:34.540
Because you know Rain would have made fun of the loser Paul.

65
00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.940
It would have been winner Paul and loser Paul.

66
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.540
You know Rain would have done that.

67
00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.700
You're so right.

68
00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.500
All right, lady.

69
00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.900
Fast fact number two.

70
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.460
This episode introduces the relationship between Kelly and Daryl.

71
00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.420
And I have to tell you, this was a very popular storyline with fans.

72
00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.880
Oh, people loved this.

73
00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:55.820
Loved it.

74
00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:56.880
I love it.

75
00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:57.700
Me too.

76
00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:03.660
I love how like no nonsense Daryl is and it spirals Kelly out.

77
00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:09.120
She does not know how to handle his just direct, honest, no game playing.

78
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:09.720
Yeah.

79
00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.460
Well, it started a number of debates online.

80
00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.740
There was Kelly and Daryl versus Kelly and Ryan.

81
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.520
There was a very short-lived Carol.

82
00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:20.260
Carol.

83
00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.980
Mashup of Kelly and Daryl.

84
00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.300
Carol with a K.

85
00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:25.560
People made jokes.

86
00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:26.900
Who will last longer?

87
00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.160
Carol or Carol.

88
00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.680
If you remember Michael's girlfriend, Carol.

89
00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:31.420
Oh.

90
00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:32.060
Yes.

91
00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:38.240
So this was just really, really fun to see this relationship play out.

92
00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.620
It was mostly like a revenge date, I think, on Kelly's part.

93
00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:44.860
But she also...

94
00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:44.910
You think?

95
00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:46.780
You think?

96
00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.080
I mean, she literally...

97
00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.480
Daryl has a whole talking head where he says, you know, I get excited when I see the

98
00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.220
little dude come in the office because that's when she pays attention to me.

99
00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.980
But she also does seem like a little taken with him.

100
00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.940
But guys, the thing about this, and a lot of people pointed this out online, is like

101
00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:08.240
finally there's a man who's treating her well and she can't deal.

102
00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.340
Like, she is attracted to the drama.

103
00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.120
She is attracted to Ryan.

104
00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:13.720
Ryan is as well.

105
00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.060
This is their downfall.

106
00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.720
We will see it play out over several seasons.

107
00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.240
Well, we all know couples like this.

108
00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:20.660
Come on.

109
00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:27.140
You have that friend who was always attracted to the guy that made her a total mess, right?

110
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:27.780
Yeah.

111
00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.420
And vice versa, right?

112
00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.380
Dudes as well.

113
00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:30.760
Yeah.

114
00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:35.280
And you'd be like, what about that other person who's so incredibly nice to you?

115
00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.020
And they're like, no, I want the person that makes my crazy.

116
00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.820
Yeah, pretty much.

117
00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:44.360
Well, there are great Kelly and Daryl scenes in this episode, but there was a deleted one

118
00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:45.140
I loved.

119
00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.720
It happens towards the end, but it's...

120
00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.760
I'll wait till we get there.

121
00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.460
But it's Kelly trying to make amends.

122
00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.820
Oh, oh, that sounds great.

123
00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:54.880
Oh, I can't wait for that.

124
00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.060
All right, lady.

125
00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.520
Fast fact number three.

126
00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.940
I don't know if you remember, Angela, but right around the time that we were filming

127
00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:06.120
this episode, Steve Carell won Best TV Actor at the Teen Choice Awards.

128
00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:07.900
No, I didn't remember that.

129
00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.300
Well, you know, you win a surfboard.

130
00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.840
That's the award.

131
00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.000
That's the award statue is a giant, colorful surfboard.

132
00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.960
Now, Steve had won a Golden Globe.

133
00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:17.300
Yeah.

134
00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.820
And we had won the SAG Award.

135
00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:20.100
But this was different.

136
00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.740
Our show had won an Emmy.

137
00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.400
Our show had won an Emmy.

138
00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.680
But this was like you've hit the mainstream.

139
00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.120
This was a big deal.

140
00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:33.760
To give you some context, here are the previous winners in Steve's category in the years prior.

141
00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:40.140
Matt LeBlanc for Friends, Ashton Kutcher, Wilmer Valderrama for That 70s Show.

142
00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.380
Then Steve won.

143
00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.200
After that, the Jonas Brothers won.

144
00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:48.100
I'm telling you, this was like Steve is a bonafide star.

145
00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.040
He's a star.

146
00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:53.000
I mean, if the teens are voting for you, come on.

147
00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:53.840
Yes.

148
00:05:54.240 --> 00:06:00.760
Well, I kind of noticed, Ange, that I feel like right around this time for all of us on

149
00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:05.900
the office, this is when I feel like our lives started to change and we are about to enter

150
00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.400
what I am calling our Hollywood years.

151
00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.380
We started having the most crazy experiences.

152
00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:11.780
Yeah.

153
00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:19.180
I mean, I remember I was standing in line for this party we'd been invited to and standing

154
00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.040
in front of me are Robert De Niro and Joe Pesci.

155
00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:22.580
Yeah.

156
00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.960
I'm waiting in a line with those guys to get into a party.

157
00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:31.020
And I remember looking at you and being like, what is happening right now?

158
00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:35.240
Jenna, I remember being at a party during the award show season.

159
00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:36.800
Brad Pitt was there.

160
00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:37.280
Oh, yeah.

161
00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:38.520
And Angelina Jolie.

162
00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:38.940
Yeah.

163
00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.880
And a Leo DiCaprio.

164
00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.240
Like, I don't know him, guys.

165
00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.220
By the way, I didn't talk to any of them.

166
00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:45.520
No.

167
00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:46.220
Because I was terrified.

168
00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:50.120
I danced in the corner with Jenna and Oscar and Jack McBrayer.

169
00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.160
That's what we did.

170
00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:57.120
Well, I just remember at this time, I was constantly calling home to tell my parents

171
00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.420
all the crazy stuff that was happening to us.

172
00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.660
And this was also when we started going on talk shows.

173
00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:03.300
Remember?

174
00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.680
And that was a whole new world.

175
00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:11.960
I remember, Angela, you were the first female cast member of The Office to go on David Letterman.

176
00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:12.680
Oh, my gosh.

177
00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.080
I was so nervous, you guys.

178
00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:15.440
I was so nervous.

179
00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:17.460
I had the runs that morning.

180
00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:18.760
It was such an overshare.

181
00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:20.360
I was so nervous.

182
00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.260
And David Letterman was so, like, kind.

183
00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.420
And his whole team there was so...

184
00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:29.420
It's like they knew I was about to poop my pants or something.

185
00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.520
I was so thrilled.

186
00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:38.680
I was such a fan of his that my sister took a photo of the TV of me on Letterman.

187
00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:39.940
And I have it in a frame.

188
00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.420
Like, that's before anything was, like, on the internet, you know?

189
00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:44.080
Yes.

190
00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.860
So she took a picture of my TV.

191
00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.880
Well, it was just such a crazy time.

192
00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:56.120
And, Ange, I'm so grateful that I got to go through all of that with you, because I

193
00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.640
feel like we had the same reaction to all of this.

194
00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:01.020
We were so tickled to be invited.

195
00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:04.380
We loved to gossip with each other about everything we saw.

196
00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:08.940
And then the next day, we woke up and we went to Target and we bought things to make a wreath.

197
00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:11.780
And our lives went on.

198
00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:12.800
Exactly.

199
00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:14.320
Oh, my gosh.

200
00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:15.360
I, yeah.

201
00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:19.940
Well, listen, when you feel like you're a fish out of water and you look over your shoulder

202
00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:24.680
and your best friend is that same fish out of water, you know, you're going to be okay.

203
00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:32.100
You know, it's like that fancy toilet that was like, remember, it was like a port-a-potty,

204
00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.900
but it was like the fanciest port-a-potty I'd ever seen.

205
00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.320
And you and I couldn't get over it.

206
00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:39.240
We are geeking out over this fancy port-a-potty.

207
00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:41.920
And I'm sure people were like, okay, ladies.

208
00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.800
And we're like, it's got lights inside.

209
00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.240
Yes, this is a thing.

210
00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:49.280
When they have these parties, they bring in these fancy toilets, you guys.

211
00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.780
We couldn't stop talking about it.

212
00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.200
We took pictures of it.

213
00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:53.660
We scrapbooked about it.

214
00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:54.260
Oh, my gosh.

215
00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:58.300
It had like a porcelain sink and it has music playing in it.

216
00:08:58.420 --> 00:08:58.660
Remember?

217
00:08:58.900 --> 00:08:58.980
Yes.

218
00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:02.540
Somehow they funneled music into this fancy port-a-potty.

219
00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:04.160
I'd never seen anything like it.

220
00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.360
This was the stuff we documented.

221
00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:12.620
Meanwhile, like other cast members on the show are like literally toasting champagne with Brad Pitt.

222
00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:17.400
And we're over taking photos of the port-a-potty and we can't stop talking about it.

223
00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:18.920
We're like, the thing you need to see.

224
00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.500
The thing we're writing home about tonight is this toilet.

225
00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:25.040
I talked in great detail with my dad about that.

226
00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:27.080
And he was like, do you have a pedal you push?

227
00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.180
I'm like, yes, dad.

228
00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.080
But it's still fancy.

229
00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.500
Oh, my gosh.

230
00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:35.720
I knew we were meant to be friends when we had to take photos with the port-a-potty.

231
00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:37.120
Same.

232
00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:41.880
Well, listen, guys, we will have more stories coming up because like I said,

233
00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:45.120
this did kick off a very fancy part of our lives.

234
00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:49.140
And it's been fun to go through my old photos and these archives.

235
00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:52.220
And I've earmarked a few more stories to tell.

236
00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:53.300
Oh, I can't wait.

237
00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:57.600
By the way, every time you say I've gone through my archives, I don't know why.

238
00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:58.940
Maybe it's because I'm loopy today.

239
00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:04.120
I just picture you like in that final scene of Raiders of the Lost Ark that somewhere in your

240
00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:10.160
garage, you have all these boxes and you're like, boop, boop, like a little mini crane going.

241
00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:15.140
Well, if only I could be that organized, it would be my dream come true.

242
00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.760
Oh, you would be so happy.

243
00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:17.300
All right.

244
00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:21.600
We will take a break and we will be back to dive into Money Part 2.

245
00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:32.500
All right.

246
00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:33.320
We're back.

247
00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:34.480
Money Part 2.

248
00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:39.100
We're starting with the scene where a very tired Pam is at front reception.

249
00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:39.980
She's yawning.

250
00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.140
Jim is yawning.

251
00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:43.040
Dwight walks in yawning.

252
00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:45.360
Everyone's kind of had a rough night.

253
00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:51.640
And Jim says to Dwight, and I wrote this down because it just goes with that argument of

254
00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:56.540
when people try to be nice to Dwight or Angela, it almost always backfires on them.

255
00:10:56.980 --> 00:11:01.060
Jim very nicely says, you okay, to Dwight, right?

256
00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:05.400
Dwight says, I am better than you have ever been or ever will be.

257
00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.320
